 All notable changes to Hearth are documented in this file.
 
@@ -139,6 +143,295 @@ preceding beta series.
 History begins at 1.5.0. For releases before 1.5.0, see the
 [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/ondreu/Hearth/releases) page.
 
+## [3.9.0]
+
+### Added
+
+- **A folder of albums can be browsed as albums.** The Music card's folder source
+  gains **Show albums**, offered once *Include subfolders* is on: the list under
+  the transport becomes those subfolders as collapsed album rows, each with its
+  track count, and opening one shows its tracks with a row back to the list \u2014
+  picking a track plays that album as the queue. Files loose in the picked folder
+  are listed last, as *Loose tracks*. With the switch off the card stays one
+  queue of every track, in name order.
+
+
+- **Hearth speaks Traditional Chinese too.** A full \`zh-tw\` locale joins English,
+  German, French, Korean and Simplified Chinese: Obsidian's own Traditional
+  Chinese (\`zh-TW\`) display language now loads it, \`zh\` stays Simplified and
+  \`zh-CN\` still falls back to it. The wording is Taiwan's \u2014 a vault is \u5132\u5B58\u5EAB \u2014
+  and the search bar understands Traditional spellings and Taiwan place names
+  next to the Simplified ones, for times, weather, Wikipedia, markets, dice and
+  currency. Simplified Chinese, German, French and English are unchanged.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- **A Music card whose folder changed no longer plays the old folder's tracks**
+  (#486). The card and the player share one queue, and the card handed its
+  tracks over only when that queue was empty: after pointing the card at another
+  folder the list showed the new tracks while next/previous still walked the old
+  queue, and a single path present in both was enough for the card to treat the
+  stale queue as its own. The player now remembers which card gave it the queue
+  and rebuilds it when that card's tracks change \u2014 keeping the track that is
+  playing, and stopping instead of playing a file that is gone.
+
+
+- **The Pet card in Terminal design no longer grows Obsidian's memory until it
+  crashes** (#479). Its frames were the one animation in Hearth running on a
+  JavaScript timer instead of CSS, and every tick rebuilt the card's whole body
+  \u2014 a span with a click and a key listener for every sprite cell \u2014 and, through
+  the board's frame layer, every frame on the board. It did that in a background
+  tab as well, where nothing can be seen: roughly 3,000 nodes and 900 listeners
+  every five seconds, climbing until the renderer died. A repaint now keeps the
+  rows whose text did not change, the frame layer is rebuilt only when something
+  drawn on it changes, and a card's own redraw is skipped while its leaf is
+  hidden. The sprite also merges neighbouring cells of one colour into a single
+  run, and the whole body is the click target, so patting it works as before.
+
+
+- **The toggles in Hearth's settings and dialogs are visible again in the TUI
+  style on Obsidian 1.15** (#480). That release gives every toggle an absolutely
+  positioned, fully transparent \`::before\` as its click area; the TUI style draws
+  the \`[ ]\` / \`[x]\` checkbox in that same pseudo-element and only set its content
+  and colour, so the label inherited \`position: absolute; opacity: 0\`, left the
+  layout, and \u2014 with \`height: auto\` on the container \u2014 the toggle collapsed to
+  0 px. The rule now puts the pseudo-element back in flow, which restores the
+  toggle at its text height.
+
+
+- **\u201CSame as the file explorer\u201D now matches the sidebar with the sidebar
+  closed** (#439). Obsidian leaves the file explorer unbuilt while the left
+  sidebar is collapsed, and the call that orders a folder answers only with the
+  tree items it has built \u2014 so the page fell back to the explorer's *sort
+  setting*, read off that same unbuilt view, which is to say alphabetical. It
+  reads the setting from the state the leaf still carries now, treats a partial
+  answer as no answer instead of pushing the rest of the folder to the end, and
+  redraws when the sidebar's answer changes \u2014 so opening the sidebar corrects a
+  page that was drawn while it was closed.
+
+## [3.8.0]
+
+### Added
+
+- **TaskChute Plus, on the board.** Three cards read
+  [TaskChute Plus](https://github.com/hiroyaiizuka/taskchute-for-obsidian)'s own
+  data instead of hosting its view: *TaskChute* lists the day's tasks in the
+  plugin's own time sections (every window drawn, empty ones included), starts
+  and stops them, adds, reorders and drags them between windows to reschedule,
+  moves, duplicates and deletes them, ticks the running clock without a repaint,
+  and moves to another day from its header \u2014 all through the plugin, so its
+  timer, log, heatmap and reminders stay in step \u2014
+  *TaskChute overview* sums up today and the last seven days, and
+  *TaskChute heatmap* draws the plugin's activity as a calendar grid of minutes.
+  The list keeps one TaskChute view mounted off-screen as its data source; the
+  other two read the plugin's monthly snapshot and mount nothing.
+
+
+- **The New-note button takes its name from the search field.** Typing a title in
+  the search bar and pressing the button beside it now creates a note called
+  exactly that, instead of one called "Untitled" and a name to type again \u2014
+  the quickest capture of something that isn't in the vault yet. Characters a
+  file name can't hold are dropped, an empty field keeps using the *Filename*
+  setting, and a search that is a filter rather than a title (\`#tag\`,
+  \`key:value\`) is left alone rather than turned into a file name. The same goes
+  for a Search bar card's button. A typed title replaces the filename pattern
+  rather than being appended to it, so no \`{{date}}\` prefix and no \`{{prompt}}\`
+  dialog appear over text you have already typed.
+
+
+- **A slideshow can rotate through notes.** The Slideshow card's *Slides from*
+  setting gains a third source beside a list and a folder of pictures: **The
+  notes in a folder**. Every Markdown note in the chosen folder \u2014 subfolders
+  optional, exactly as for pictures \u2014 is drawn as a page with the same renderer
+  the embed and daily cards use, so links, callouts, embeds and checkboxes work
+  as they do in the note. A long note scrolls inside the card, and *Fit* and
+  *Slow zoom* are left out of the settings because a note has no picture to fill
+  or zoom. Ordering, the timer, once-a-day and by-hand advances, the caption and
+  the open button all work the same on a notes card. The card is also offered
+  twice in the *Add card* picker \u2014 as **Slideshow** and as **Notes slideshow**,
+  which starts on this source \u2014 and the picture entry's one-line description now
+  names notes too, so the source is visible before the settings dialog.
+
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Spacing is now a three-step choice.** *Settings \u2192 Hearth \u2192 Dashboard* (and
+  each board's Layout tab, and the setup wizard) used to offer *Compact
+  spacing* as an on/off switch; it is now *Spacing* \u2014 *Roomy*, *Compact*, or
+  the new *Flush*, which drops the side and bottom gutters so the board and its
+  cards run to the edge of the pane. A flush board also ignores the *Content
+  width* ceiling, which would otherwise leave a centred column with side
+  margins of its own. The top of the page, the gap under
+  the header and the card insets keep the compact rhythm. An existing vault
+  keeps exactly the spacing it had, because the old setting is folded into the
+  new one when settings load. The space *between* cards is part of their saved
+  layout rather than a style, so Flush leaves it untouched.
+
+
+### Fixed
+
+- **Editing a card no longer rebuilds the board under the cursor** (#475). A
+  couple of seconds into typing into a card's embedded editor \u2014 a note or a
+  base \u2014 the whole board re-rendered, the editor came back at the top with the
+  caret gone, and the scroll position was lost. The boards subscribe to
+  \`MetadataCache\`'s \`resolved\` event to catch up on frontmatter that arrives
+  after they were first drawn (#399), but Obsidian also fires that event after
+  *every* file modification, so the autosave that follows a pause in typing
+  counted as "the cache just warmed up" and re-rendered everything. The
+  catch-up now runs once, for the cold cache a startup board was drawn
+  against; later metadata changes arrive through *Live refresh on vault
+  changes*, which is debounced and held while you are typing.
+
+- **The Quick switcher engine ranks a note by its name, the way the switcher
+  it copies does** (#447). Searching "black sphinx" listed an empty note called
+  "A" from a folder of that name above the note actually called "Black Sphinx":
+  the query was matched against the whole path, so a folder name scored exactly
+  like a file name, and equal scores were settled alphabetically. The name is
+  matched on its own now, a match that only found the folder is ranked below
+  every name match, ties keep the order the vault returns instead of being
+  re-sorted, and files excluded from link suggestions are down-ranked. The
+  attachment types the switcher itself lists are complete again (\`.oga\`,
+  \`.opus\`, \`.tiff\`), and a file type brought by a plugin (\`.excalidraw\`,
+  \`.typ\`, \u2026) is listed when Obsidian can display it, as the switcher does.
+  For the same query the order and the scores now line up
+  with Obsidian's own switcher.
+
+
+- **The Git card works again with obsidian-git 2.41.** That release moved its
+  commit-and-push actions, which every earlier version kept flat on the
+  plugin, onto its own GitActions helper, so Hearth's support probe, which
+  read the old flat names, decided the actions weren't there and disabled the
+  commit, sync, push, pull, fetch, discard-all and branch buttons under
+  *This version of the Git plugin doesn't support that*. The write actions
+  are now looked up per member, on the helper first and on the plugin itself
+  second, so a 2.41+ and a pre-2.41 install answer alike.
+
+
+- **The commit scope the card editor chooses is respected again on
+  obsidian-git 2.40 and later.** Since 2.40 renamed its commit options to
+  \`mode\`, Hearth kept sending the \`onlyStaged\` boolean those builds never
+  read, so *Smart*, *All* and *Staged* were all collapsing to the plugin's
+  default (\`all\`). The card now names the scope, and dispatch translates it
+  into both dialects: \`mode\` goes to obsidian-git 2.40+, where *Smart*
+  passes through and the plugin resolves it exactly as its own Commit
+  command does, against a status read at commit time; the old \`onlyStaged\`
+  rides alongside for builds that predate modes.
+
+
+- **Staging everything from the card no longer rests on a possibly stale
+  snapshot.** Stage-all and unstage-all now run without a status, matching
+  what obsidian-git's own source-control view does: on desktop both stage
+  and reset the whole tree regardless, and on mobile the working tree is
+  re-read at the moment of the click.
+
+## [3.7.0]
+
+### Added
+
+- **A hotkey that puts the cursor in the board's search field.** *Focus board
+  search* is bindable under Settings \u2192 Hotkeys: a board that is already in front
+  only takes the cursor, one that is open behind a note is brought forward
+  first, and with no Hearth tab at all it opens one. The existing *Focus search
+  on open* setting keeps covering only a board that is opening.
+- **A Music card, playing from the vault or from a Navidrome/Subsonic server.**
+  Two sources behind one card. *Vault folder* takes every audio file in a folder
+  (optionally including subfolders), *Vault files* a hand-picked list, and both
+  play through Hearth's own player \u2014 one \`<audio>\` for the whole plugin, so the
+  music carries on through a redraw of the board instead of stopping every time
+  you change a setting. *Stereo* plays nothing itself: it is a remote control for
+  the Stereo plugin's player, showing the track, the queue and the transport, so
+  a library kept on a server needs no second queue. Transport, seek, volume,
+  shuffle and repeat (off / whole queue / this track), the queue on the card, and
+  a remembered playhead between sessions. Four layouts rather than one skin:
+  *Classic* is the row of text with the queue under it, *Medium* puts a square
+  artwork beside the details, *Full artwork* makes the artwork the card with the
+  controls on a scrim, and *Large artwork* gives the artwork half the card and
+  the details and queue the other half. The vault has no album art, so the
+  artwork is a record that spins while playback runs \u2014 a CSS animation, so the
+  board's motion gates freeze it. Every layout adapts to the card's own size
+  (container queries): the queue, then the seek row, then the volume drop out as
+  the card gets shorter, so a small card is a player rather than a clipped one.
+  On the Expressive design the artwork, play button and queue take the design's
+  accents. Playback always starts paused.
+
+- **A video as the board's backdrop** (#416). *Vault video* joins the background
+  types: point it at an MP4 or WEBM in your vault and the board sits behind a
+  muted, looping clip instead of an animated GIF or WEBP. The decode happens off
+  the main thread, which is the reason those animated images stuttered \u2014 but a
+  clip is still the most expensive backdrop Hearth paints, so it is the one kind
+  the performance tier decides for you, and the setting says so where you choose
+  it. On *Full* it plays. From *Balanced* down it holds still on its first frame
+  \u2014 a still picture rather than a black hole \u2014 and the *Minimal* tier replaces
+  it with its flat colour like every other backdrop. A paused clip is also what
+  a reader whose system asks for reduced motion gets, and it stops whenever the
+  window it sits in is not the one being used.
+
+- **A heatmap card can pick its own colour** (#430). The grid used to be tinted
+  with Obsidian's global accent, which a low-saturation theme makes almost the
+  same shade as an empty square. *Grid \u2192 Color* in the card's settings tints the
+  squares with a colour of your own, on either design, while the fade from one
+  note to many stays as it was; leaving it alone \u2014 or pressing the reset button \u2014
+  keeps following the theme's accent. Two grids tracking different things can now
+  look different. Shade and darkening modes are not part of this change.
+
+- **Hiding a filter chip can now hide the type from search too** (#434). A chip
+  hidden under *Settings \u2192 Search \u2192 Filter chips* used to vanish from the row
+  while search kept returning that kind of file, which read as the setting not
+  working. The new *Search only the shown types* switch (off by default) turns
+  the row into a whitelist: results hold nothing but the types whose chips are
+  shown, every chip counts as picked, and switching one off narrows the search
+  further. It is per board as well, and a Search bar card can turn it on for its
+  own bar. Every engine follows it \u2014 the built-in search, note-body matches,
+  Omnisearch, the Quick switcher and the recents list.
+
+- **A folder can be opened in Obsidian's own file explorer** (#448). Three
+  places, one destination: the Folder card's *Opening a subfolder* dropdown
+  gains *In the file explorer* beside its browser and in-card choices, the
+  Bookmarks card gains one setting \u2014 *Opening a folder bookmark*, in the folder
+  browser (the default, unchanged) or in the file explorer \u2014 and a launchpad
+  button can be a **Folder**, with the card's own *Opening a folder button*
+  setting choosing between the browser and the sidebar the same way. Both
+  settings are one dropdown in the card's settings, and the launchpad's appears
+  only once the card has a folder button, so nothing new is drawn on any board.
+  Revealing puts the folder in the sidebar, opening the explorer there if it was
+  closed. The reveal is the core file explorer's own \`revealInFolder\` \u2014
+  undocumented, so when it can't be done (plugin off, or the internal changes
+  shape) the click opens Hearth's folder browser instead of doing nothing.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **\u201CSearch filters\u201D is now \u201CFilter chips\u201D**, the name the per-board override
+  already used. What it controls is the row of chips, not which files are
+  searched; the new switch above is the one that decides the latter.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- **A board with a card holding several views no longer jumps to that card**
+  (#440). Opening the dashboard, or switching one of the card's views, left the
+  board where it was until the switcher was drawn \u2014 and then the board scrolled
+  down to bring the row of tabs into view, even when the row was nowhere near
+  the edge. The row scrolls sideways when there are more tabs than fit, so it is
+  the row that is moved now, and the board is never asked to move at all. A board
+  that had already saved the jump as its position keeps it until it is scrolled
+  back to the top once; nothing else is needed.
+
+- **A folder browser tab keeps its own page across a restart** (#439). Opening a
+  folder in a tab and sorting it by date came back after a restart on the same
+  folder, but sorted the explorer's way again: the folder reached the tab's view
+  state, the sort only reached a debounced layout save. Both go the same way
+  now. The sections folded while reading are remembered as well \u2014 on the device,
+  so a folder folded in one browser is folded in the next one and after a
+  restart, without writing to \`data.json\`.
+
+- Currency conversion no longer hangs on a single host, and no longer forgets
+  its rates between sessions. The rates are the ECB's own daily reference file,
+  asked first, with Frankfurter's mirror only as a fallback, and the last good
+  table is kept on the device \u2014 so a restart or an offline session converts with
+  the rates it already had instead of reporting that none are available. Both
+  are asked at their canonical address (the old \`api.frankfurter.app\` host only
+  redirects now). BGN left the supported units, as the ECB stopped publishing a
+  rate for the lev when Bulgaria adopted the euro (#422).
+
 ## [3.6.0]
 
 ### Added
